From 3f8e5f8d48b03fe3479bd199522354ad5cf50791 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:13:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] VPVulkan + SPIR-V: native motion vectors for VPKTAA
 (vpvk/motion.h)

Source 2 never renders motion vectors; VPEngine generates them.

Translator (SpirvLowerOptions::motion): the vertex entry point is lowered twice into one shader,
first with every constant buffer (uniform blocks, push constants) and, optionally, read-only
storage buffer (bone palettes) read from "slot + base" where the driver binds the previous
frame's bytes, then normally; both clip positions leave at locations 30/31. Side effects in the
first run (memory or image writes, atomics) refuse the variant. The fragment variant reads them
and writes cur - prev Vulkan NDC to an extra RG16F colour output.

Driver: with vpvk_config_set_motion_vectors(1) (or VPVK_MOTION=1) before vkCreateDevice:
- multiview pipelines with depth, single sample and a free trailing colour slot get a
  format-only variant (motion attachment declared, not written) and, when opaque (depth test +
  write, no blend), a motion variant; dynamic colour write masks apply to both;
- every multiview pass whose draws all have variants gets the motion target (RG16F 2D array,
  pass size, 4 rotating textures) as one more colour attachment: cleared to 60000 (invalid) by
  the eye frame's first pass (depth cleared) and loaded by the rest;
- a motion draw binds, next to its current buffers, the bytes the same draw (pipeline + vertex/
  index buffers + ranges + occurrence in the frame) read the previous eye frame; the bytes of
  this frame, read from unified memory at vkQueueSubmit, are kept for the next (two arenas,
  swapped per eye frame). First sighting: current bytes (zero motion that frame).
- vpvk_motion_get(serial, &info): newest complete frame (or one serial): id<MTLTexture>, size,
  layers, scale (0.5, 0.5: NDC -> uv), invalid threshold, serial, completion.
Motion includes camera motion (the game's own matrices).

Tests: gpu_spirv.motion (variant lowering), gpu_vulkan.motion (pass gets the target, variants,
previous bytes bound, vpvk_motion_get).

