+// VPEngine motion vectors for VPKTAA (VPVulkan). Plain C: Klepton (C) and Swift call it.
+//
+// When enabled (before vkCreateDevice), every multiview eye pass with a depth attachment and a free
+// colour slot gets one more colour attachment, an RG16Float 2D-array texture of the pass's size
+// (layer = view = eye). Opaque draws in those passes run a variant of their pipeline whose vertex
+// shader computes the position twice, once with the previous frame's copy of every uniform block and
+// push constant range it reads (same draw: same geometry, same occurrence in the frame), and whose
+// fragment shader writes (current - previous) Vulkan NDC there. Blended and depth-write-off draws
+// leave it alone; pixels no opaque motion draw covered keep the clear value (invalid).
+//
+// Values: texel.xy * scale = (current - previous) in uv units of the pass's viewport (+x right,
+// +y down, the texture's row 0 is the top). Camera motion INCLUDED (the game's own matrices), and
+// so is any projection jitter difference between the two frames. |texel.x| >= invalid_threshold:
+// no motion known there (use depth + poses). A draw seen for the first time gets zero motion for
+// that frame (its previous data does not exist yet).
+#pragma once
